{
  "description": "Synthetic OSV records and the identity-edge fields a conforming OSV collector must write on the vulnerability.cve payload. aliases, related and upstream are each trimmed, de-duplicated and SORTED (ascending, byte order); blank entries are dropped. aliases and related are always written: an empty list is written as JSON null, not omitted and not []. upstream is written ONLY when it has at least one non-blank id after cleaning; otherwise the key is absent. upstream is a DIRECTED edge (a downstream distro record naming the CVEs it repackages): it is never an alias, is never folded into aliases or correlation_anchors, and never selects cve_id. A distro bundle of CVEs (for example a DSA that lists the CVEs it fixes) must therefore be expressed as upstream, not as aliases. status is written as \"withdrawn\" only when the record carries a non-blank withdrawn timestamp; an active record has NO status key. Each case lists its own expected_absent_payload_keys. Required rule shapes are derived from the cases' own records by the fixturepack test.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "aliases_only",
      "record": {
        "schema_version": "1.6.0",
        "id": "GHSA-bbbb-0001-0001",
        "modified": "2026-10-29T00:00:00Z",
        "aliases": ["CVE-2026-2001"]
      },
      "expected": {
        "advisory_id": "GHSA-bbbb-0001-0001",
        "aliases": ["CVE-2026-2001"],
        "related": null
      },
      "expected_absent_payload_keys": ["upstream", "status"]
    },
    {
      "name": "related_only",
      "record": {
        "schema_version": "1.6.0",
        "id": "GHSA-bbbb-0002-0002",
        "modified": "2026-10-29T00:00:00Z",
        "related": ["GHSA-bbbb-0009-0009"]
      },
      "expected": {
        "advisory_id": "GHSA-bbbb-0002-0002",
        "aliases": null,
        "related": ["GHSA-bbbb-0009-0009"]
      },
      "expected_absent_payload_keys": ["upstream", "status"]
    },
    {
      "name": "upstream_only_distro_record",
